      {
        "id": "N003",
        "kind": "internal",
        "statement": "U has a K-basis of length n=ell+1, dim_K U=n>0, and U≠0. The function F is a unital ring homomorphism End_Z(M)→End_K(U), with F(f)(a⊗m)=a⊗f(m). The map S:V_K→U is K-linear, has inverse S_inv, and hence is a K-linear isomorphism. V_K≠0. For every f∈End_Z(M), S∘ind(f)=F(f)∘S. Consequently S transports invariant subspaces for any such pair of operators bijectively, and transports zero and whole spaces to zero and whole spaces.",
