          "id": "S001",
          "text": "H003 gives lambda=(ell:Z) and ell<p. Since p is prime and char K=p (H001,H002), M003 at r0=ell gives that red(ell!) is a unit, hence nonzero in the field K. For j∈Fin(n), M004 at (ell,j) gives c_j j!(ell−j)!=ell!. After applying red this is red(c_j) red(j!) red((ell−j)!)=red(ell!)≠0. No factor of a nonzero product in a field can be zero, so red(c_j)≠0 for every j. The finite product red(Dprod)=∏_j red(c_j) is nonzero.",
