          "text": "Let W be any K-linear subspace of U and temporarily assume L2: W is invariant under F(x_M),F(y_M). By induction it is invariant under every power of each operator, with the identity as the base. Linearity of W and F003 give invariance under F(X_M(r)),F(Y_M(r)) for all r≤ell. The factors in A_ij=X_M(ell−i)Y_M(ell)X_M(ell)Y_M(ell−j) all have indices between 0 and ell, so their F-images preserve W by composition and the ring-homomorphism laws. Finally multiplication by red(c_j)^(-1) preserves W because W is K-linear. Thus every T_ij preserves W. Discharge L2 and universally quantify W. Along with F001,F002 this proves the full reduced matrix-unit and stability statement; Lie invariance has never been used to infer stability of divided powers of index at or above p.",
